course: dictionary
lesson: 12323
title: Names and place words: costa
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names. A name often starts with a capital letter and points to one special thing, such as one shop, one country or one person. «Costa» is one of these words, so check the clues around it before you look for a meaning.
explain: «We queued at Costa for two hot chocolates.» Costa has a capital letter, and you queue and buy drinks there, so it is a shop. Here Costa means Costa Coffee, a chain of coffee shops, not the word coast. Ask yourself: is this a name for one special thing?
explain: «Costa Rica has rainforests, volcanoes and toucans.» Here Costa is part of a place name. Costa Rica is the name of one country, so Costa on its own does not mean the whole country. Look at the words next to it.
fact: Costa is usually a name: of a coffee shop, a country, a holiday coast or a person.
fact: Costa Coffee is a big chain of coffee shops in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Costa Rica is a country in Central America, famous for rainforests, volcanoes and wildlife such as sloths and toucans.
fact: Costa del Sol and Costa Brava are holiday coasts in Spain.
fact: In Spanish, Portuguese and Italian, «costa» means «coast», but it is not a common English word.
exercise: «We queued at Costa for two hot chocolates.» What does Costa mean here? | A type of sloth | Lost in the rain | *A big chain of coffee shops | A tall mountain
exercise: «Our holiday was on the Costa del Sol in Spain.» What kind of place is the Costa del Sol? | A rainforest | A volcano | A coffee shop | *A holiday coast
exercise: «Costa Rica has rainforests, volcanoes and toucans.» What is Costa Rica? | *A country in Central America | A bird with a huge beak | A coffee shop in London | A holiday coast in Spain
test: «Diego Costa scored a goal for his team.» In this sentence, Costa is | A coast | *A surname | A volcano | A coffee shop
test: «In Spanish and Italian, «costa» means «coast».» What does costa mean in those languages? | *Coast | Coffee | Sloth | Volcano
exam: Which word in «Let's go to Costa and then visit Costa Rica» names a coffee shop? | Let's | Rica | *Costa | Visit
